1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:26,000
SPEAKERA: So where on the staircase does he catch up?

2
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:56,000
SPEAKERA: People often say Zeno thought infinitely many pieces must add up to something infinite.

3
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:26,000
SPEAKERA: In Simplishius's report, his worry is that it is impossible to traverse an infinite number of things in a finite time.

4
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:56,000
SPEAKERA: And that's a much harder question.

5
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:26,000
SPEAKERA: Zeno's dichotomy makes the same point, without any tortoise.

6
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:56,000
SPEAKERA: So to run a hundred metres, first run half of it. Then half of what's left, then half of that.

7
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:26,000
SPEAKERA: After ten halvings, you've run all but one part in a thousand and twenty-four, and less than ten centimetres is left.

8
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:56,000
SPEAKERA: Like a to-do list that grows exactly as fast as you work through it.

9
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:26,000
SPEAKERA: Then the run has no first step at all. So how does it ever begin?

10
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:56,000
SPEAKERA: Zeno's arrow attacks motion from the other side, by cutting time into instants.

11
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:26,000
SPEAKERA: In that instant, it fills a space exactly its own size, so it isn't moving.

12
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:56,000
SPEAKERA: That one is slippery.

13
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:26,000
SPEAKERA: The modern answer treats speed at an instant as a limit.

14
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:56,000
SPEAKERA: And in a hundredth, half a metre. Distance over time stays at fifty metres a second, however short the interval.

15
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:26,000
SPEAKERA: So the speed at an instant is defined as that limit.

16
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:56,000
SPEAKERA: It sounds almost too simple.

17
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:26,000
SPEAKERA: The front block of one row passes every oncoming block, but only half of the still ones.

18
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:56,000
SPEAKERA: Half equals double? That can't be right.

19
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:26,000
SPEAKERA: Simplishius tells a story. When Diogenes the Cynic heard Zeno's arguments, he said nothing, stood up, and walked.

20
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:56,000
SPEAKERA: Honestly, it's tempting.
